# make_item_icons.gd
# Dev tool, not part of the game: draws placeholder icons for the items v3 stat items (flat pixel art,
# 16 x 16 scaled to 64 px, a dark outline added round the shape, like the other placeholder icons) and
# writes textures/ui/items/<id>.png. Each item is a shape template drawn in its own colour (ItemData.color)
# plus an accent. Icons that already exist are left alone unless --force is given.
#   Godot_v4.7.2-stable_win64.exe --headless --path . --script res://tools/make_item_icons.gd [-- --force]
# Then run --import once so Godot picks the new PNGs up.

extends SceneTree

const N := 16
const SCALE := 4
const OUTLINE := Color("17131f")

# Template characters: . empty, 1 the item's colour, 2 lighter, 3 darker, a the accent, g / G steel,
